,title,link,text,language,family
0,Eskayan language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eskayan_language,"Eskayan is an artificial auxiliary language of the Eskaya people of Bohol, an island province of the Philippines. Its grammar is structurally similar to Visayan-Boholano, the native language of Bohol, with a lexicon that shows little relationship to any Philippine languages. [2][3][4] While Eskayan has no mother-tongue speakers, it is taught by volunteers in at least three cultural schools in ...",Eskayan,Mixed language
1,Eskayan script - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eskayan_script,"Eskayan is the constructed script of the auxiliary Eskayan language of the island of Bohol in the Philippines. Like Yugtun and Fox script, it is based on cursive Latin.",Eskayan,Mixed language
2,Eskayan - Department of Linguistics - UP Diliman,https://linguistics.upd.edu.ph/the-katig-collective/language-capsules/eskayan/,"The word made flesh: An ethnographic history of Eskayan, a utopian language and script in the southern Philippines [Unpublished dissertation]. Australian National University. 10.25911/5d5147de68750 Kelly, P. (2015). A comparative analysis of Eskayan and Boholano-Visayan (Cebuano) phonotactics: Implications for the origins of Eskayan lexemes.",Eskayan,Mixed language
3,"Eskayan Language (ESY) – L1 & L2 Speakers, Status, Map ...",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/esy/,Eskayan is a dormant language of the Philippines. It is a mixed language. The language is no longer used as a first language by any remaining members of the ethnic community. It is not known to be taught in schools.,Eskayan,Mixed language
4,Eskayan script and language - Omniglot,https://www.omniglot.com/writing/eskayan.htm,"The Eskayan people speak Cebuano as their everyday language and use Eskayan for prayers, songs and formal speeches. Eskayan is written with a syllabic script consisting of over 1,000 symbols, some of which are shown below. The symbols are apparently modelled on human body parts, though resemble cursive Latin letters.",Eskayan,Mixed language
5,The Astonishing Origins of a Rebel Language in the ...,https://www.shh.mpg.de/2152072/the-astonishing-origins-of-a-rebel-language-in-the-philippines,"Apr 7, 2022 · The Last Language on Earth examines the origins and history of the Eskayan language, spoken today by an upland community on the island of Bohol in the southern Philippines. Using linguistic, ethnographic and historical lines of investigation, the new book engages directly with the Eskayan language itself, as well as the direct perspectives of those who use it today.",Eskayan,Mixed language
6,OLAC resources in and about the Eskayan language,http://www.language-archives.org/language/esy,"Other resources about the language ONLINEEskayan: a language of Philippines. n.a. 2018. SIL International. oai:ethnologue.com:esy ONLINELINGUIST List Resources for Eskayan. Damir Cavar, eLinguistics Foundation Board Member (editor); Malgorzata E. Cavar, Director of Linguist List (editor). 2022-05-31.",Eskayan,Mixed language
7,Eskayan | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/esy/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..WiP4X3g-GfrqfPhbUCAuXw9uX0p2PSzh59P2x1dq144,Eskayan is a dormant language of the Philippines.This graph shows the vitality of Eskayan. Institutional — The language has been developed to the point that it is used and sustained by institutions beyond the home and community.,Eskayan,Mixed language
8,OLAC resources in and about the Eskayan language,http://olac.ldc.upenn.edu/language/esy,"ONLINEAudio and video recordings of Eskayan singing, language lessons and hermeneutics in Biabas on 23 May 2010..",Eskayan,Mixed language
9,The origins of invented vocabulary in a utopian Philippine language,https://www.benjamins.com/catalog/aplv.2.1.03kel,"The utopian Eskayan language and script has been spoken for at least three generations by a small community on the island of Bohol in the southern Philippines. Speakers, who use the language in special domains, attribute its creation to a legendary ancestor known as Pinay.",Eskayan,Mixed language
